  "title": "Periodic walls that avoid their own copies decide every direction",
  "subject": "When a three-place contact of a twisted fair world contradicts along a class, and which bending contacts are selective on every torus",
  "conclusion": "For every three-place tiling contact with a constant frame, a direction has an assignment exactly when some periodic wall crosses its cylinder without meeting its own copies; the rule needs no determinism, because a cylinder with an assignment has a periodic one. Planted staircases make eight of the twelve bending contacts selective on every torus with sides at least 3; for the other four, good walls must sometimes repeat a state, and selectivity on every torus is open.",
